1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Rotate Array — LeetCode 189

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,600
Problem: rotate the array to the right by k steps, in place — the last k values wrap around to the front.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,850
Example: nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], k = 2

4
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:11,900
Result: [4, 5, 1, 2, 3] — rotated right by 2

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:16,550
Hint: rotating right by k moves the last k values to the front — three reversals do exactly that, in place

6
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:21,450
Approach: reverse the whole array, then the first k, then the rest (with k %= n first)

7
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:25,350
k %= n handles the case where k is larger than n

8
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:30,190
Step 1: reverse the whole array → [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]

9
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:34,270
Step 2: reverse the first k = 2 → [4, 5, 3, 2, 1]

10
00:00:34,270 --> 00:00:37,910
Step 3: reverse the rest → [4, 5, 1, 2, 3]

11
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:41,040
Done — rotated right by 2

12
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:44,590
[4, 5, 1, 2, 3], rotated in place. Time O(n), space O(1)

13
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:49,700
